!!! 02-bindings-and-types.matrix
!!! Scalars, bindings, casts, arrays and raw pointers.
!!!
!!! Matrix keeps Ny's scalar contract exactly: wrapping integer arithmetic at
!!! the resolved width, promotion order real > long > integer > byte, and
!!! byte storage that retains the low eight bits.

book tour.values

main returns number begin paragraph

    !!! Three kinds of binding. "is" declares and initialises; "set ... to"
    !!! mutates an existing binding. Ny spells both of these "=".
    value   limit   as number is 10        !!! immutable
    variable total  as number is 0         !!! mutable
    constant MARGIN as number is 3         !!! compile-time constant

    set total to total plus 1

    !!! Every scalar type Matrix spells. There is deliberately no spelling
    !!! for i8, i16, u16, u32, u64 or f32: Ny rejects their arithmetic.
    value count    as number is 42
    value population as number  is 10000000000
    value flag     as override byte    is 255 becomes override byte
    value fraction as floating    is 0.5
    value ready    as boolean is true
    value label    as text    is "dispatch"
    value hex      as number is 0xFF

    !!! "converted to" is a cast. "as" is a type annotation. Ny spells both
    !!! "as", which hides whether a value changed representation.
    value widened  as number    is count becomes number
    value truthy   as boolean is count becomes boolean

    !!! Word operators, conventional precedence: times/over/remainder bind
    !!! tighter than plus/minus. Parentheses group.
    value area     as number is limit times limit
    value average  as number is (count plus limit) over 2
    value leftover as number is count remainder limit
    value negated  as number is minus count

    !!! Comparisons and logic.
    value in_range as boolean is count is at least 0 and count is at most 100
    value exact    as boolean is count equals 42
    value differs  as boolean is count does not equal limit
    value either   as boolean is ready or in_range
    value inverted as boolean is not ready

    !!! Bitwise operations require integer operands.
    value masked   as number is count bitwise and 0x0F
    value flipped  as number is count bitwise xor 0xFF
    value doubled  as number is count shifted left by 1
    value halved   as number is count shifted right by 1
    value complement as number is bitwise not count

    !!! Dynamic arrays. Indexing reads with "at"; writing is a "set"
    !!! statement. An out-of-range read yields the element's zero value and
    !!! an out-of-range write is a no-op, exactly as in Ny.
    variable values as array of number is [1, 2, 3]
    set values at 1 to 7
    say values at 0

    !!! "len" and "push" are compiler builtins on an array receiver, not
    !!! library functions, and they take positional arguments with no declared
    !!! parameter names. Matrix gives them dedicated spellings rather than a
    !!! "with ... being ..." clause that would have nothing to bind against.
    say the length of values
    append 9 to values

    !!! Raw pointers. Allocation and release are explicit statements.
    allocate buffer as pointer to number sized 2
    set buffer at 0 to 40
    set buffer at 1 to MARGIN
    say (buffer at 0) plus (buffer at 1)
    release buffer

    !!! say takes exactly one value. Use separate statements for several, and
    !!! say "" for a blank line.
    say widened
    say fraction
    say label
    say ""

    give 0
end paragraph
